WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.103
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.103 --> 00:00:04.480
about Data Fusion, new cloud
certifications, and Google

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.302
Cloud Next 2020.

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:08.260
I'm Mark Mirchandani,
and welcome to "This Week

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.860
in Cloud," where we serve
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.620
Cloud Data Fusion is our
fully managed data integration

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.860
service that simplifies how
you authenticate, monitor,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.360
and protect your data.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.030
And we've just released new
beta features, such as support

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.028
for VPC service controls.

00:00:24.028 --> 00:00:26.320
Check the blog for an overview
of the built-in features

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.140
working to keep your data safe.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.900
Last September, we announced
improvements to the Cloud Build

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.120
GitHub app, making it
easier for developers

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.340
to trigger builds on
specific branches, pull

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.888
requests, or tags.

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:40.180
We're happy to announce that
those features are all now

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.650
generally available.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.270
Go try them out.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.420
For 2020, we've got two
new certification programs.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.430
The Google Cloud
Certified Fellow

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.040
is an invitation-only
certification program

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.350
for technical leaders
designing enterprise solutions

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.730
with Anthos.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.590
Through a series of
assessments and labs,

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.840
the program will identify
experts who can effectively

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.840
lead organizations through
frictionless hybrid multi-cloud

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.010
adoption.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.640
And the Professional Cloud
DevOps Engineer Certification

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.160
enables cloud professionals
to demonstrate their expertise

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.070
in development operations
and service reliability

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.062
to employers.

00:01:13.062 --> 00:01:15.520
Check them out if you're looking
to add more certifications

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.470
to add to your collection.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.290
We just announced the dates
for Google Cloud Next 2020.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.150
Join us in San Francisco
or online April 6

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.570
through April 8 for
some Google Cloud magic.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.237
Registration is now open

00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:29.320
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.550
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:32.810
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.430
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.990
We'll see you in the cloud.

